course: dictionary
lesson: 4953
title: Impurity: the unwanted bit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An impurity is a small amount of something unwanted that is mixed into something that should be pure. Pure means clean, with nothing else in it. Dirt in water is an impurity.
explain: «Water with impurities (tiny bits of other things mixed in it), like tap water, can conduct electricity, so water and electricity are dangerous together.» The brackets tell you the meaning: impurities are tiny bits of other things. Impurity can also mean the state of not being pure.
explain: Context clues help here too. Words like remove, contain and free from show what impurities do and how people deal with them. Scientists remove impurities by filtering, sieving or evaporating, and you can check the meaning by swapping in your own words.
fact: An impurity is a small amount of an unwanted substance mixed into something pure.
fact: Impurities can often be removed by filtering, sieving or evaporating.
fact: Water treatment plants remove impurities to make water safe to drink.
fact: In metals and gems, impurities can change the colour or strength.
fact: Useful phrases: remove impurities, contain impurities, free from impurities.
exercise: What is an impurity? | *A small amount of an unwanted substance mixed into something pure | A bright colour painted onto a jar | A type of kitchen filter | A large, clean piece of metal
exercise: Which method can remove impurities from water or salt? | Painting | *Filtering | Whistling | Counting
exercise: «Water with impurities can conduct electricity.» What can the impurities make water do? | Glow in the dark | *Conduct electricity | Freeze instantly | Turn into metal
test: Why do water treatment plants remove impurities? | To make water heavier | To add colour to water | To turn water into metal | *To make water safe to drink
test: In metals and gems, what can impurities change? | *Colour or strength | The weather outside | The name of the owner | The day of the week
exam: Which phrase means having no unwanted bits in something? | Remove impurities | Impurities of the sea | *Free from impurities | Contain impurities
